/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Term Frequency-Inverse Document Frequency \(TF-IDF\) has been one of the most widely used techniques in information retrieval. It calculates the importance of a word in a document relative to a corpus and helps rank documents based on keyword overlap. While TF-IDF is fast and interpretable, it cannot capture contextual meaning, distinguish between polysemous words, or identify synonymous phrases.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [3]
