249 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (This section outlines the complete pipeline developed for the hybrid document search system. Our methodology comprises four primary stages: data preprocessing, semantic vector representation, model training and evaluation, and performance assessment.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
250 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (4.1 Data Preprocessing)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
251 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The data preprocessing stage was essential to ensure that the documents were properly prepared for vectorization and semantic encoding. The system was designed to support both PDF and plain text \(.txt\) files. For PDF files, textual content was extracted using the PyPDF2 library. Non-PDF documents were read using chardet-based encoding detection to accommodate various character encodings such as UTF-8 and ISO-8859-1.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
252 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Once the raw text was obtained, standard text normalization was performed. This included lowercasing, removal of extra whitespaces, and elimination of non-alphanumeric characters. Documents with insufficient textual content were filtered out. Tokenization was performed later during TF-IDF vectorization and BERT encoding using their respective tokenizers.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
253 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (4.2 Semantic Vector Representation)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
254 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (To support both lexical and contextual understanding of text, we implemented two parallel vectorization strategies.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
255 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 461 0 R
/E <>
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
256 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 462 0 R
/E (BERT Embeddings: For semantic encoding, we used a pre-trained BERT model \(bert-base-uncased\) from the Hugging Face Transformers library. The model generated a 768-dimensional dense vector for each document using mean pooling over the final hidden state. These embeddings allowed us to measure the contextual similarity between a user query and candidate documents using cosine distance.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
257 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (4.3 Model Training and Hybrid Search Logic)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
