/E (4.4 Performance Evaluation)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [16]
>>
endobj
265 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (We evaluated the model using a combination of qualitative assessments and response-time benchmarks. Test queries were run in three configurations: TF-IDF only, BERT only, and the hybrid pipeline. Results were reviewed manually to assess semantic alignment with the queries. The hybrid model consistently retrieved more relevant documents than TF-IDF alone, and did so more efficiently than a full BERT-based search.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [17]
>>
endobj
266 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Average query latency was significantly reduced due to the TF-IDF filtering step, making the system scalable for larger document sets. This methodology demonstrates how hybrid search models can balance accuracy and efficiency in real-world document retrieval applications.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [18]
>>
endobj
267 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (4.3 Model Training and Evaluation )
/E (4.3 Model Training and Evaluation )
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [18]
>>
endobj
268 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The final phase of our methodology focused on building and evaluating a hybrid document retrieval model that integrates traditional keyword-based search with deep contextual understanding. The model leverages both TF-IDF and BERT to rank documents in response to user queries, optimizing for accuracy, relevance, and scalability.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
