286 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (4.3 Model Training and Evaluation )
/E (4.3 Model Training and Evaluation )
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
287 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (To assess the effectiveness of our hybrid document retrieval system, we conducted a multi-dimensional performance evaluation. The core goal was to determine how well the combination of TF-IDF and BERT balances speed, relevance, and contextual understanding when compared to using either technique independently.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
288 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (We focused on four key evaluation aspects: \(1\) Top-K Relevance, which measures how contextually relevant the top retrieved documents are to the input query; \(2\) Precision at K, which considers the fraction of retrieved results that are semantically meaningful; \(3\) Inference Time, to assess the average latency per query; and \(4\) Subjective User Quality, based on human assessment of search outputs.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
289 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (To conduct this evaluation, we created a test suite of fifteen diverse user queries across domains such as law, education, healthcare, and technology. Each query was executed using three configurations: TF-IDF-only filtering, BERT-only semantic ranking, and the combined hybrid approach. Returned results were reviewed and scored by multiple evaluators based on how relevant they were to the query intent.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
290 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The results showed that TF-IDF alone was fast but often returned documents that were only partially relevant, especially for queries involving abstract or indirect language. BERT-only retrieval produced highly accurate results due to its deep semantic understanding but was significantly slower, as it required computing embeddings for the entire corpus.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
291 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The hybrid approach delivered the best of both worlds. It filtered the candidate documents using TF-IDF, reducing the search space, and then re-ranked this subset using BERT embeddings. This process not only improved semantic accuracy but also reduced inference time substantially compared to a full BERT-only pipeline.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
292 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E <>
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
293 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Overall, the evaluation confirmed that our hybrid document search engine is highly effective for real-world use. It balances performance and precision, scales well with document volume, and provides a solid foundation for intelligent, context-aware document retrieval.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
